From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RicemanRhys <176650384+RicemanRhys@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 08:01:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Local-only: 5.1 output through XAudio2 when asked for and the
 device has the speakers

RECOMP_SPEAKERS=5.1 opens the default device's mastering voice at its own
channel count; if its speakers include FL FR C LFE and a surround pair, a
6-channel source voice (FL FR C LFE BL BR) is mapped onto them with an
explicit matrix (surrounds to the side pair when there is one). Otherwise
stereo, exactly as without the switch. The DSP stage then writes the speaker
bins to their channels and the HRTF submix bins to their corners at the
stereo gain (mixdown_51), and the monitor submits six channels.
mcpx_apu_output_channels() reports the result. Checks: RECOMP_APU_FORCE_51=1
opens 5.1 on any device; RECOMP_APU_OUT_WAV=PATH writes what the monitor
submits. Default: unchanged (crash_twoc notes 18.58).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
